s  fans were hopeful and vocal about a  long-awaited sequel to 2010's skate  three so to see this coming directly  from an EA figurehead  sounded like all of our dreams were  coming true especially after the  backlash of Activision's Tony Hawk's Pro  Skater 5 this was the best time for EA  to give the hands what they wanted sadly  a few days later CEO of EA Andrew Wilson  killed everyone's buzz by stating there  were no plans to make skateboard fans  were and still are devastated to make  matters worse in 2018 EA reopened the  skate 2 &amp; 3 online servers before their  press conference at e3 the timing seemed  right for EA to discuss a skate comeback  why else will they do something like  that well skate was not discussed that  day and since then fans and trolls alike  have been asking about skateboard across  all of EA social media when I heard this  I thought it was a joke but no if you go  on to any one of their posts you will  see a comment section flooded with skate  for comments will EA ever give in to the  demands of fans or will they behave like  that teacher that doesn't begin the  lecture until the class completely  quiets down now wait Jack Dunn  after the critical successes of the  grand theft auto and Max Payne series  Rockstar Vancouver and Rockstar North  launched bully in 2006 while it didn't  do gangbusters at launch when compared  to other rockstar titles it got plenty  of attention selling 1.5 million copies  in its first two years despite the usual  controversy Rockstar titles faced at  launch the game attained a cult  following and fans were eager for a  follow up title what we got instead was  an HD remaster in 2008 and a mobile port  in 2016 this one is a little harder to  gripe about because it appeared that a  sequel was in the works shortly after  the release of Red Dead Redemption in  2010 rockstar began to work on bully 2  according to an article by a video game  chronicle the sequel was being worked on  for 18 months before being cancelled in  2013 unfortunately this was also around  the time Rockstar Vancouver the original  development team closed its doors in  2012 despite all of the setbacks and  being shelved rumors continued to pile  up online about an eventual return to  Bulworth Academy we all know how  tight-lipped Rockstar can be for better  or worse so all we can do is wait what  do you think will come first bully 2 GTA  6 or Rockstar table-tennis 2  that's it for our list feeling angry sad  or just old me too and I know there were  several other games considered so if you  want to see more mournfully click that  like button and I'll be back to ruin  your day faster than you can say left 4  dead 3 until then  mope with me in the comments spam FS to  pay respects and I'll see you next time  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

